notes="This very pale leaf asks when the exterior product on cycles extends to a partial differential-algebra structure, draws the lifting diagram for sigma_ij and records an indeterminacy Hom group. The upper second factor in the diagram is visibly C^j, while the lower sources have Z^j; this distinction is retained even though a uniform cycle factor would make the intended lifting picture more immediate. The middle product is a cross, whereas the other rows use circled tensor signs. In the Hom display the ink favors Z^{i+1}, not H’s C^i. Conditional on the expected short exact sequence C^i/Z^i isomorphic Z^{i+1}, two lifts with the same lower restriction and upper differential differ by a map from Z^{i+1} tensor Z^j to Z^{i+j}; right-exactness of tensor supplies that quotient. This explains the displayed group but is not a proof that lifts exist. The lower direct-sum / homotopy-or-homology assertion is not checked: the faint prose and unspecified differential do not warrant a stronger conclusion. The final oval resembles a more than zero and is left explicitly doubtful. A blue arrow below the direct-sum sign and the opening parenthesis are retained. H’s following section heading is editorial and absent from the sheet. Manuscript foot 353; no date."
